  "_note": "D70: the CLOSED set of 'this is somebody's name' sentences, as DATA. plugins/_shared/name_spans.py compiles it. It is read from the ORIGINAL text before translation, so a name is learned and protected in Telugu script, romanized Telugu (Tenglish), Devanagari and romanized Hindi (Hinglish). To teach JARVIS a new way of saying it, add a word to a list or a template here; no code changes. Latin-letter words are matched without regard to case; a Latin NAME must start with a capital letter unless the template says lower_ok (then the name word 'peru'/'naam' must be in the sentence). Native-script words are matched as written. Written by Claude, NOT checked by a native speaker (D70).",
